    questions: [{"prompt":"Which approach best matches the goal of this lesson (Rewrite quadratics in vertex form by completing the square.)?","choices":["Apply “Completing the Square” with clear structure and a checked result.","Guess from memory of the lesson title only.","Skip checks because the first answer looks neat.","Ignore domain restrictions and sign errors."],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"College-ready algebra shows structure and verification, not guessing.","order":1},{"prompt":"The solutions of (x − 4)(x − -3) = 0 are:","choices":["x = -4 and x = 3","x = 1 only","x = -12 only","x = 4 and x = -3"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Zero product property: each factor can be zero.","order":2},{"prompt":"Which vocabulary idea is most central to Unit 2 (Quadratic Functions) as used in “Completing the Square”?","choices":["random guessing","skipping the diagram","vertex","discriminant"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Unit 2 leans on precise use of “vertex.”","order":3}],
