    questions: [{"prompt":"Which approach best matches the goal of this lesson (List outcomes systematically; use fundamental counting.)?","choices":["Ignore domain restrictions and sign errors.","Apply “Counting & Sample Spaces” with clear structure and a checked result.","Guess from memory of the lesson title only.","Skip checks because the first answer looks neat."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"College-ready algebra shows structure and verification, not guessing.","order":1},{"prompt":"Which habit best prevents the common mistake: Adding probabilities that are not mutually exclusive without inclusion…?","choices":["Erase all work whenever unsure.","Trust the first answer if it is an integer.","Name the structure, compute carefully, then check with substitution or an inverse.","Change the problem until an easier number appears."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Error prevention is structural, not cosmetic.","order":2},{"prompt":"Which vocabulary idea is most central to Unit 9 (Probability & Statistics) as used in “Counting & Sample Spaces”?","choices":["independent","random guessing","skipping the diagram","sample space"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Unit 9 leans on precise use of “sample space.”","order":3}],
