    questions: [{"prompt":"Which approach best matches the goal of this lesson (Interpret fit quality without overclaiming causation.)?","choices":["Ignore domain restrictions and sign errors.","Apply “Regression Literacy” with clear structure and a checked result.","Guess from memory of the lesson title only.","Skip checks because the first answer looks neat."],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"College-ready algebra shows structure and verification, not guessing.","order":1},{"prompt":"Which habit best prevents the common mistake: Forcing a linear fit on clearly curved data, or claiming causation fro…?","choices":["Erase all work whenever unsure.","Trust the first answer if it is an integer.","Name the structure, compute carefully, then check with substitution or an inverse.","Change the problem until an easier number appears."],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Error prevention is structural, not cosmetic.","order":2},{"prompt":"Which vocabulary idea is most central to Unit 10 (Functions, Modeling & Capstone) as used in “Regression Literacy”?","choices":["inverse","random guessing","skipping the diagram","domain"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Unit 10 leans on precise use of “domain.”","order":3}],
